From 85cdd32995f3bb89af2315965325ec92ad011a4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 12:57:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tfa9872: stop claiming nxp,tfa9874

sound/soc/codecs/ carries a dedicated tfa9874 driver, and this one lists
nxp,tfa9874 in its match table as well. Two drivers matching one
compatible is a race the board cannot win: whichever binds first takes
the part.

On the OnePlus 7T Pro, which has two of these amplifiers, this driver won
both of them and then overwrote its own widgets, because it registers the
same DAPM names for every instance:

  tfa987x 2-0034: Chip revision: 0x0c74
  tfa987x 2-0035: Chip revision: 0x0c74
  tfa987x 2-0035: ASoC: sink widget PWUP overwritten
  tfa987x 2-0035: ASoC: sink widget Speaker overwritten

Both chips answer on I2C and the card enumerates, but no audio reaches
the speakers: the routing collapses onto one set of widgets and the
driver that was validated on this hardware never binds.

Leave nxp,tfa9874 to the driver written for it. This can be claimed again
once the widget names are per-instance.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c
index 26bed43059941..682346a010f12 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c
@@ -299,7 +299,20 @@ static int tfa987x_i2c_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 
 static const struct of_device_id tfa987x_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "nxp,tfa9872" },
-	{ .compatible = "nxp,tfa9874" },
+	/*
+	 * nxp,tfa9874 is deliberately not claimed here. sound/soc/codecs/
+	 * carries a dedicated tfa9874 driver, and two drivers matching one
+	 * compatible is a race the board cannot win: whichever binds first
+	 * takes the part. On a board with two of these amplifiers this one
+	 * won and then overwrote its own DAPM widgets --
+	 *
+	 *   tfa987x 2-0035: ASoC: sink widget PWUP overwritten
+	 *   tfa987x 2-0035: ASoC: sink widget Speaker overwritten
+	 *
+	 * -- because it registers the same widget names for each instance.
+	 * The speakers went silent. Claim it again once the widget names are
+	 * per-instance and the tfa9874 driver can retire.
+	 */
 	{ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, tfa987x_of_match);
